<title>CHILE: Chile's Madeco sets up Uruguay unit.</title>
<headline>Chile's Madeco sets up Uruguay unit.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper products maker Madeco SA said it has created a new division to sell its products in Uruguay and neighboring countries.</p>
<p>Madeco, which already has investments in Argentina and Peru, said its Ingewall division has bought a Uruguayan company that will be renamed Ingewall Uruguay SA.</p>
<p>&quot;This company will allow Ingewall to venture with greater ease in its area of business in Uruguay and in neighboring countries,&quot; said the company in a statement to the Securities Superintendency.</p>
<p>The new firm will produce aluminium products.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212</p>
